  abstract = {The linking number is the simplest link invariant given by Gauss; it is the first Gauss diagram formula expressed by one arrow among two circles. Proceeding the next stage, we study the second Gauss diagram formula consisting of two arrows among two circles. We call a function of this type the multiple linking number. There are two multiple linking numbers; one of them is ordinary Vassiliev invariant and the other function is surprisingly sensitive to the necessity of the second Reidemeister moves though any one-component Gauss diagram formula cannot detect the necessity.},
