  date = {2023},
  url = {https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.13398},
  urldate = {2024-06-26},
  abstract = {In 2017, Jones studied the unitary representations of Thompson’s group FFF and defined a method to construct knots and links from FFF. One of his results is that any knot or link can be obtained from an element of this group, which is called Alexander’s theorem. On the other hand, Thompson’s group FFF has many subgroups and it is known that there exist various subgroups which satisfy or do not satisfy Alexander’s theorem. In this paper, we prove that almost all stabilizer subgroups under the natural action on the unit interval satisfy Alexander’s theorem.},
